Package: datasus
Type: Package
Title: An Interface to DATASUS System
Version: 0.16.0
Authors@R: person("Renato", "Prado Siqueira", email = "rpradosiqueira@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: It allows the user to retrieve the data from the systems of 
    DATASUS (SUS IT department related to the Brazilian Ministry of Health, 
    see <https://datasus.saude.gov.br/informacoes-de-saude-tabnet/> for more
    information) much in the same way that is done in the online portal.
    It provides access to vital statistics from SIM and SINASC, hospital
    production and morbidity from SIH/SUS, ambulatory production from
    SIA/SUS, the National Registry of Health Establishments (CNES),
    resident population estimates, notifiable conditions from SINAN,
    legacy immunization and nutritional surveillance series, cancer
    screening and diagnostic exams, historical SUS financing tables, and
    modern surveillance microdata published by OpenDataSUS, including
    ESAVI, e-SUS influenza-like illness, individual PNI doses and COVID-19
    hospital occupancy, and record-level DBC/DBF files from SIM, SINASC and
    SIH/SUS. Curated schemas, selective columns, multipart downloads and
    chunk processing support memory-efficient analysis of large files. It also
    provides validated grouped rates, proportions, ratios, case fatality,
    confidence intervals, population-denominator joins, epidemiological
    weeks, moving averages, direct age standardization and ready-made
    standard populations.
    An offline IBGE territorial reference supports current municipality,
    state and region codes, DATASUS code conversion, territorial joins and
    completion of geographic time series.
